--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Description:
This directory holds the x86_64 libv4lconvert and libv4l2 sources (from
v4l-utils). They build as libnvv4lconvert.so and libnvv4l2.so.

libnvv4l2 is the userspace V4L2 wrapper used by the gst-v4l2 plugin
(nvv4l2decoder in libgstnvvideo4linux2.so). It links against
libnvv4lconvert, which converts pixel formats the camera does not expose
natively.

The library sources are LGPL-2.1-or-later. This README is Apache-2.0.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Platform:
x86_64 only. Both Makefiles stop on any other architecture, including Jetson.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pre-requisites:
- DeepStream SDK installed (default install path below must exist)
- gcc
- Build and install libv4lconvert before libv4l2. libnvv4l2.so links
  -lnvv4lconvert and looks for it in ../libv4lconvert and in the install dir.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Build order:
  1. libv4lconvert/   -> libnvv4lconvert.so
  2. libv4l2/         -> libnvv4l2.so
  3. ../gst-v4l2/     -> libgstnvvideo4linux2.so (needs libnvv4l2.so installed)

See libv4lconvert/README and libv4l2/README for the per-library steps.
build/build.sh follows this same order on x86.
